**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A material imported from a user's glass catalogue says which file, and which bytes of it, it came from (the S13.2 brief 'A user-supplied .agf file becomes user materials ... with imported-from-file provenance'; 001 §B 'provenance — built-in / user / imported-from-kit / pulled-from-source'; step 405's precedent: add a provenance case where none fits). None fits: `UserProvenance` carries nothing and `SourcePullProvenance` names an online source, its licence and its snapshot (`LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, steps 24, 91, 405, 441). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `EntryProvenance` gains a seventh case, `FileImportProvenance of EntryFileImportInfo`, declared together with `and EntryFileImportInfo = { file : FileName; fileHash : ContentHash }`: the imported file's leaf name (`FileName.leafName`) and the SHA-256 of its bytes (`ContentHash.ofBytes`, step 123). An imported entry belongs to the user: `protection` answers `UserManaged`, `categoryOrigin` `UserCategory`, and `attributionOpt` (step 113) `None`, because a user's file carries no licence the app knows. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (steps 63, 91, 405): `kindValue` answers 7 for a file import and `catalogueIdOpt` `None`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (steps 30, 91, 405, 441): the provenance definition gains a seventh shape, exactly what the serializer writes for `FileImportProvenance`: `file` a non-empty string and `fileHash` the content-hash definition the file holds. The entry schemas keep version 1, because no entry file has been released (.spec-md §7). Any other complete match on `EntryProvenance` that FS0025 reports answers a file import as it answers `UserProvenance`. No other case, member, converter or schema changes; the glass import builds the case (step 463). (4) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` also covers a `FileImportProvenance` of `FileName "test-glasses.agf"` and the hash of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc`: `UserManaged` and `UserCategory`; its `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` (step 113) answers `None` for it. `EntryFileJsonTests`' `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` gains a material under that provenance; it round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers the material.

**Acceptance.** After the provenance lands, `EntryProvenance` MUST hold `FileImportProvenance of EntryFileImportInfo` (the file's leaf name and its bytes' hash), user-managed with no attribution, stored with provenance kind 7 and no catalogue, and written and read back in an entry file under `library-common.schema.json`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the widened `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed`, `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` and `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
